     3	Committed to git before the first held-out episode is run. Anything below that changes later is listed in a dated
     4	"Deviations" section at the end; nothing above it is edited.
     5	
     6	## Question
     7	Under the same on-device budget (one screenshot per step, Q4_K_M GGUF, llama.cpp, our harness), does our final LFM3
     8	model match GUI-Owl-1.5-2B on AndroidWorld? "Match" = non-inferiority with margin 8 tasks per 116 (6.9 pp).
     9	
    10	## Arms
    11	* **GUI-Owl matched**: `run_aw.py --agent=guiowl --guiowl_images=1 --guiowl_max_pixels=1048576`, GUI-Owl-1.5-2B-Instruct
    12	  Q4_K_M + Q8_0 mmproj, plus the device's installed-app list in its instruction (mirrors the input v4 receives).
    13	* **LFM3 final**: v4 (prompt v4 with installed-app list) if it passes the development gate below; otherwise v3 and v1
    14	  are reported (v1 = best seed-30 model; neither receives an app list, which can only favour GUI-Owl).
    15	* **LFM3 v1** (reference, original prompt).
    16	GUI-Owl's native-configuration number (67.9% published, own harness) is shown next to the matched number, never in
    17	place of it.
    18	
    19	## Protocol (all arms)
    20	AndroidWorld commit 55ddaf5 + local patches, Pixel 6 API 33 arm64 AVDs, 116 tasks, `n_task_combinations=1`,
    21	10x task-complexity step budget, success only if the agent ended the episode (`suite_utils.py`), temperature 0,
    22	one parse retry (LFM3). Primary score: full successes (`is_successful >= 1`, exception = failure) over 116.
    23	Secondary: official rule (exceptions dropped). Infrastructure crash before step 1 (emulator/adb, not model output)
    24	is re-run once; everything else counts.
    25	
    26	## Seeds
    27	Development: 30 (already used to choose v1/v2/v3 — not evidence for the final claim).
    28	Held-out, sealed: **7, 1234, 2026**, run in that order. Seed 7 runs tonight for GUI-Owl matched and LFM3 v1; the final
    29	LFM3 model runs seed 7 after it is frozen. Sealed = results written under `results/androidworld_sealed/`; run logs are
    30	filtered so per-task outcomes are not printed; only episode counts are inspected until every arm on a seed has
    31	finished. 38 of the 116 templates are seed-invariant; results on the 78 seed-varying templates are reported separately.
   100	  Gate inputs are now also bound to the pinned v3 run (sha256 of its 116 episode files), the generate.py manifests
